\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The motif dictionary. Top: the canonical segment clusters drawn in hit space (dots are hits, lines are segments; green true, red false). Middle: the compatibility graph each one forms, which is the object that carries the eigenvalues. Bottom: the exact eigenvalue lines each motif contributes, from the closed forms of section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:toy:spectrum}, at $s=\gamma +\delta =4$; a solid line is a bright mode and an open circle a dark one (section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:toy:modes}), with multiplicity marked where lines coincide. Every false family's \emph  {bright} lines sit close to, but never on, the four true-track lines (green dotted), except for the spectral twins of section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:comb:limits}; the lines that do fall on $\lambda =s$, from the triple and the hub, are dark and carry no amplitude.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:motifs}{{8}{19}{The motif dictionary. Top: the canonical segment clusters drawn in hit space (dots are hits, lines are segments; green true, red false). Middle: the compatibility graph each one forms, which is the object that carries the eigenvalues. Bottom: the exact eigenvalue lines each motif contributes, from the closed forms of section~\ref {sec:toy:spectrum}, at $s=\gamma +\delta =4$; a solid line is a bright mode and an open circle a dark one (section~\ref {sec:toy:modes}), with multiplicity marked where lines coincide. Every false family's \emph {bright} lines sit close to, but never on, the four true-track lines (green dotted), except for the spectral twins of section~\ref {sec:comb:limits}; the lines that do fall on $\lambda =s$, from the triple and the hub, are dark and carry no amplitude.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
