\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The two preparations of figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:circuits}, drawn out. (a) PREP on the index register: one uniformly controlled $R_y$ per qubit --- a filled square marks a uniform control, meaning one angle for each value of the qubits above, so level $j$ carries $2^{j}$ angles and the cascade $2^{m}-1=63$. The states $|\Phi ^{(j)}\rangle $ are eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:preptree}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}. (b) The angles are read off the binary tree of subtree norms; the numbers are those of the production comb ($d=40$, $m=6$), and the grey branch is the $23$ index states above $k=40$, which carry no coefficient and are dropped. (c) The system register needs no loader at all: $\mathbf  {b}$ is uniform. PREP$^{\dagger }$ in figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:circuits}(c) is the same cascade run backwards with the unsigned angles. The cascade was validated against the coefficient vector to $10^{-16}$, with and without the signs.\relax }}{23}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:prep}{{10}{23}{The two preparations of figure~\ref {fig:circuits}, drawn out. (a) PREP on the index register: one uniformly controlled $R_y$ per qubit --- a filled square marks a uniform control, meaning one angle for each value of the qubits above, so level $j$ carries $2^{j}$ angles and the cascade $2^{m}-1=63$. The states $|\Phi ^{(j)}\rangle $ are eq.~\eqref {eq:preptree}. (b) The angles are read off the binary tree of subtree norms; the numbers are those of the production comb ($d=40$, $m=6$), and the grey branch is the $23$ index states above $k=40$, which carry no coefficient and are dropped. (c) The system register needs no loader at all: $\mathbf {b}$ is uniform. PREP$^{\dagger }$ in figure~\ref {fig:circuits}(c) is the same cascade run backwards with the unsigned angles. The cascade was validated against the coefficient vector to $10^{-16}$, with and without the signs.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
