\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces The two response functions against the populated spectrum ($s=4$). (a) The 1BQF cosine: one zero, placed on the isolated-false line; the bright lines of the coupled false motifs (pair, triple) sit on the slopes and pass. (b) The degree-40 line comb: passes at the four true-track lines only, with the isolated, pair and triple lines all rejected.\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:responses}{{11}{24}{The two response functions against the populated spectrum ($s=4$). (a) The 1BQF cosine: one zero, placed on the isolated-false line; the bright lines of the coupled false motifs (pair, triple) sit on the slopes and pass. (b) The degree-40 line comb: passes at the four true-track lines only, with the isolated, pair and triple lines all rejected.\relax }{figure.caption.17}{}}
