\newlabel{tab:realisations}{{2}{31}{The three realisations of the degree-40 comb, with HHL and the one-bit filter for reference. Ancillas are beyond the system register $n_{\rm sys}=\lceil \log _2 4T^{2}\rceil $; ``calls'' counts uses of the primitive per shot before amplification; ``exact'' says whether the circuit applies the intended response exactly or through an approximation (the finite clock for HHL, the per-pair product for $e^{-iAt}$). The block encoding's own price is a separate axis, section~\ref {sec:qsvt:resources}.\relax }{table.caption.25}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The two realisations of the comb not drawn in figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:circuits}. (a) The phase sequence, eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:qsvt}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}: the block encoding $U$ and its inverse alternate with rotations $e^{i\phi _kZ}$ on a signal qubit, each conditioned on the dilation qubit reading $|0\rangle $; $d$ calls, $d{+}1$ phases, and the polynomial appears on the real part of the post-selected branch. (b) The trigonometric comb on the one-bit filter's own primitive: $K$ controlled evolutions $e^{\mp iAt}$ interleaved with rotations $e^{i\varphi _kX}$ on one ancilla, post-selected on zero, at the width of the 1BQF. The states $|\Phi _k\rangle $ and $|\Theta _k\rangle $ mark the same three stages as in figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:circuits}: prepared, transformed, post-selected.\relax }}{32}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:circuitsqsvt}{{16}{32}{The two realisations of the comb not drawn in figure~\ref {fig:circuits}. (a) The phase sequence, eq.~\eqref {eq:qsvt}: the block encoding $U$ and its inverse alternate with rotations $e^{i\phi _kZ}$ on a signal qubit, each conditioned on the dilation qubit reading $|0\rangle $; $d$ calls, $d{+}1$ phases, and the polynomial appears on the real part of the post-selected branch. (b) The trigonometric comb on the one-bit filter's own primitive: $K$ controlled evolutions $e^{\mp iAt}$ interleaved with rotations $e^{i\varphi _kX}$ on one ancilla, post-selected on zero, at the width of the 1BQF. The states $|\Phi _k\rangle $ and $|\Theta _k\rangle $ mark the same three stages as in figure~\ref {fig:circuits}: prepared, transformed, post-selected.\relax }{figure.caption.26}{}}
