\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Qubit and depth scaling against matrix size $N=4T^{2}$ (tracks per event on the top axis), in the presentation of the predecessor papers. (a) Logical qubits: exact staircases $\lceil \qopname  \relax o{log}_2N\rceil +$constant for HHL with a full-precision clock ($2\lceil \qopname  \relax o{log}_2N\rceil +2$) and with an eight-bit clock, the comb on a block encoding (LCU $+7$, phase sequence $+4$), and the comb over $e^{-iAt}$ and the one-bit filter, which coincide at $+2$; the faint lines add the $45$ workspace qubits of the hit-priced block encoding. The box lists the counts at the HL-LHC-scale event, $T=1500$. (b) Two-qubit gates per shot: calls per shot times gates per call, with the measured Givens-product price $152\,T^{1.37}$ for the evolution-based routes (open markers beyond the measured range, $T>400$) and the hit-oracle model $103\,T^{0.85}$ for the block-encoding routes.\relax }}{35}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
