\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {27}{\ignorespaces Fitting the response to the measured pile-up (heavy $T=200$): (a) exact per-mode false (red) and true (green) formation weight against $\lambda $, with the fitted response overlaid; the fitted roots land on the pair and triple lines. (b) The resulting efficiency/false-rate frontier, with the twin fragments biting only above $\ensuremath  {\varepsilon _{\rm  seg}}\approx 0.99$. (c) False rate at matched efficiency $0.985$ for the base and fork systems (three-event means). (d) The same quantity for responses fitted directly at fixed polynomial degree: production-scale degrees already realise the measured optimum (section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:limits:realizability}).\relax }}{49}{figure.caption.39}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fit}{{27}{49}{Fitting the response to the measured pile-up (heavy $T=200$): (a) exact per-mode false (red) and true (green) formation weight against $\lambda $, with the fitted response overlaid; the fitted roots land on the pair and triple lines. (b) The resulting efficiency/false-rate frontier, with the twin fragments biting only above $\eff \approx 0.99$. (c) False rate at matched efficiency $0.985$ for the base and fork systems (three-event means). (d) The same quantity for responses fitted directly at fixed polynomial degree: production-scale degrees already realise the measured optimum (section~\ref {sec:limits:realizability}).\relax }{figure.caption.39}{}}
