\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {32}{\ignorespaces The motif dictionary of figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:motifs} under each operator, from the closed forms of sections\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:occupancy}--\ref  {sec:fork} (grey: base-$A$ positions). The fork moves only the competing-pair lines ($s\pm \beta $); occupancy shifts the true chains rigidly by $+4\alpha $ and splits the same-role pair to $s+2\alpha $, $s+6\alpha $; the same-role $k$-clique line $s+4\alpha +2\alpha (k{-}1)$ (purple) grows linearly with hit degree and sets the spectral span.\relax }}{54}{figure.caption.45}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:linesmod}{{32}{54}{The motif dictionary of figure~\ref {fig:motifs} under each operator, from the closed forms of sections~\ref {sec:occupancy}--\ref {sec:fork} (grey: base-$A$ positions). The fork moves only the competing-pair lines ($s\pm \beta $); occupancy shifts the true chains rigidly by $+4\alpha $ and splits the same-role pair to $s+2\alpha $, $s+6\alpha $; the same-role $k$-clique line $s+4\alpha +2\alpha (k{-}1)$ (purple) grows linearly with hit degree and sets the spectral span.\relax }{figure.caption.45}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {33}{\ignorespaces Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:responses}'s question asked of the fitted responses: $|p(\lambda )|$ per operator (rep-0 universal response, moderate noise) against that operator's exact motif lines. The fork system's response concentrates into a single dominant pass — the term has simplified the spectrum the fit must explain. The occupancy responses live on a span-widened domain (insets; the motif window is the shaded sliver), so their $d{=}80$ passes are visibly coarser inside it — the resolution cost $\mathrm  {span}/d$ paid for breaking the twins.\relax }}{55}{figure.caption.46}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:respmod}{{33}{55}{Figure~\ref {fig:responses}'s question asked of the fitted responses: $|p(\lambda )|$ per operator (rep-0 universal response, moderate noise) against that operator's exact motif lines. The fork system's response concentrates into a single dominant pass — the term has simplified the spectrum the fit must explain. The occupancy responses live on a span-widened domain (insets; the motif window is the shaded sliver), so their $d{=}80$ passes are visibly coarser inside it — the resolution cost $\mathrm {span}/d$ paid for breaking the twins.\relax }{figure.caption.46}{}}
