\newlabel{fig:budget}{{34}{55}{(a) The efficiency lost at the $1\%$ false-rate budget, per operator (fitted response at its best degree), decomposed into its three named channels: twin loss, ripple loss, and threshold-overlap loss. On base $A$ the entire deficit is twin loss — spectral twins, irreducible for any response. (b) The twin fraction of true segments per operator (log scale): the operator sets the twin population; the response cannot touch it.\relax }{figure.caption.47}{}}
