\citation{camps2023}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {37}{\ignorespaces The rows of table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:resources} against track count. (a) Logical register width: all constructions follow $\lceil \qopname  \relax o{log}_2 4T^2\rceil $ plus a constant: the 1BQF and DSS--QETU comb lines coincide exactly (the comb pays no width for its degree on this primitive), while the dense-dilation LCU pays $+5$ and the HHL clock band $+7$ to $+9$. (b) Measured two-qubit gate cost per shot: the shared evolution call grows as $\approx T^{1.4}$ (pair count $\times $ ladder length), the three algorithms sitting at fixed multiples of it (2, 40, $\approx 130$--$510$ calls). The green diamonds are the largest single per-cluster instance at each $T$: set by the local cluster size, not by $T$, the flat exception to every other curve's growth.\relax }}{62}{figure.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rescmp}{{37}{62}{The rows of table~\ref {tab:resources} against track count. (a) Logical register width: all constructions follow $\lceil \log _2 4T^2\rceil $ plus a constant: the 1BQF and DSS--QETU comb lines coincide exactly (the comb pays no width for its degree on this primitive), while the dense-dilation LCU pays $+5$ and the HHL clock band $+7$ to $+9$. (b) Measured two-qubit gate cost per shot: the shared evolution call grows as $\approx T^{1.4}$ (pair count $\times $ ladder length), the three algorithms sitting at fixed multiples of it (2, 40, $\approx 130$--$510$ calls). The green diamonds are the largest single per-cluster instance at each $T$: set by the local cluster size, not by $T$, the flat exception to every other curve's growth.\relax }{figure.caption.52}{}}
